WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:01.775
- [Narrator] This is coffee.

00:00:01.775 --> 00:00:02.714
This is coffee being poured into

00:00:02.714 --> 00:00:05.408
the most iconic cup in
New York City history.

00:00:05.408 --> 00:00:09.158
So, how did they sell
over a billion of these?

00:00:12.624 --> 00:00:15.072
This is Leslie Buck, a Holocaust survivor.

00:00:15.072 --> 00:00:16.824
Immigrating to New York
after World War II,

00:00:16.824 --> 00:00:18.618
he got a job working as a sales manager

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.164
at the Sherri Cup Company.

00:00:20.164 --> 00:00:22.856
The company wanted to break
into the New York diner scene.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.134
Leslie noticed Greeks
ran most of the diners.

00:00:25.134 --> 00:00:26.318
So, what did he do?

00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:27.619
He decided to create and design a cup

00:00:27.619 --> 00:00:29.128
that would appeal to them.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:31.580
He used the colors of the
Greek flag, blue and white.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:33.413
Along the top is a Greek key,

00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:35.696
one of the most iconic
designs in architecture.

00:00:35.696 --> 00:00:37.692
The sides mimic a Grecian vase.

00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:39.488
Smack dab in the middle,
Greek-style lettering

00:00:39.488 --> 00:00:41.936
that embodied the very
soul and motto of the cup.

00:00:41.936 --> 00:00:43.974
We are happy to serve you.

00:00:43.974 --> 00:00:45.444
And, guess what, it worked.

00:00:45.444 --> 00:00:47.240
Solo bought the Sherri Cup Company.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.505
In 1994 alone, they sold
over 500 million cups.

00:00:50.505 --> 00:00:52.262
And, today, the Anthora cup has reached

00:00:52.262 --> 00:00:54.179
full-blown icon status.

00:00:55.031 --> 00:00:56.364
Nice work, guys.

